	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Commands

**j** - Search Jira issues
Shows cached results and searches live API in parallel. Prefix with ! to search all projects.

**ju** - Force cache update
Updates cache immediately instead of waiting for auto-refresh.

## Setup

Set these in workflow environment variables:

- JIRA_DOMAIN - Your Jira subdomain
- JIRA_USERNAME - Your email
- JIRA_TOKEN - API token from https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens

Optional:
- CACHE_QUERY - JQL for what to cache (default: your assigned tickets)
- CACHE_REFRESH_MINS - How often to refresh (default: 5)
- LIVE_SEARCH_BASE_JQL - Scope for live searches (default: your projects)
- JIRA_ORDER_BY - Sort order for results (default: updated DESC)

## How it works

Cache updates automatically every 5 minutes when you search. Live search has 3 stages:
1. Check for exact ticket key (CPR-123)
2. Search with base JQL filter
3. Fallback to broad search if nothing found

Results from cache are filtered out of live results to avoid duplicates.

## Examples

JIRA_ORDER_BY values:
- updated DESC (most recently updated first)
- created DESC (newest tickets first)
- priority DESC, updated DESC (high priority, then by update time)
- key ASC (alphabetical by ticket key)</string>
